Right.  If you get an early wand of wishing, your goal is to maximize
your chances of surviving to the Castle--you have a chance to
eliminate all those deaths that early characters who lack MC3, PR, and
other fairly common but quite valuable resources are susceptible to.

Aside: Slot management is quite important to me. I usually want the
amulet slot for "ESP unless I'm a ranger/knight/etc (telepathy-
granting quest artifact class) as ESP will stop you from getting into
those lifesave situations and will give you a heads up about grievous
non-"oLS situations (mind flayer around the corner, things like that)

Less applicable in this case, but if you get one early wish (a lamp or
smoky potion or something) then it may go for GDSM in which case
you're probably using the amulet slot for "oReflection unless you get
tons of spare wishes.

My ideal use of slots is usually:
"oESP
MR-granting artifact (possibly the Eye, which is also "ESP)
=Conflict and =Free Action, with =Levitation available (substitute
=telecontrol until I get it intrinsic)
SDSM
HoBrilliance
T-Shirt
Robe
Jumping Boots
GoDexterity
Small shield (if a non-twoweaponing class)
Lenses/towel as needed.

Some classes (e.g. high-level wizards) may substitute another cloak.

I rarely get all of those; in a SDSM setup, fallbacks include CoMR (if
I lack the artifact) or any MC3 cloak (elven/protection are best), any
old helm (preferrably elven leather, but my last game I found a +5
orcish on DL2 or so that I wore through ascension)--telepathy is nice
and would cause me to wear "oLS--speed boots (I'll try like mad to
polypile or wish up jumping before the run though), leather gloves.

In a GDSM setup I go with "oReflection and still prefer brilliance
over telepathy.

Shield is always small unless a shield of reflection is my only
reflection source.  I'll almost always abandon GoPower for leather in
the mid-late game--I'll wear dex if I found them but they're far from
critical.  Expert dagger/dart-throwers who I'm playing as machine-
gunners might be an exception.



